        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In addition to these annual feasts, there were the weekly Sabbaths to be observed, commemorating God’s rest from creation, and also the redemption from bondage in Egypt (Deut. 5:15). On these days the daily sacrifices were doubled, the loaves of the shewbread were changed, and the people abstained from all manner of work and a holy assembly was held. See Sabbath.",
      "references": [
        {
          "text": "Deut. 5:15",
